{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue",{"I left the good dishes in the cabinet, stupid thing to think about","I can still smell my mother's kitchen, cinnamon and bacon grease","I left my guitar behind, I think about it every night","My dog used to wait by the door every evening, I hope someone's feeding him","I left the back porch light on, isn't that stupid?","My mother's kitchen smelled like cornbread and Pine-Sol, I'd give anything for that smell","I can still hear the screen door slamming, every summer, a slap and a squeak","Had a swing set in the yard, my kids loved it, I wonder if the swings are still swinging","I never even said goodbye to the house, I just left, I just ran"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=raider,outlaw,gang,club,crime,prison",{"My trailer had air conditioning - real AC","I miss my recliner - don't laugh"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","",{"I miss my own bed so much it hurts","Home, I used to just call it the house, now it's HOME","My front porch, I'd give anything to sit on it again","The smell of my mother's kitchen, I'd know it anywhere","Remember the sound of the screen door? I miss that sound","My dog used to meet me at the gate, every single day","Sunday supper, the whole family around one table","My room, my posters, my stupid little desk, I miss it","That creaky stair, third from the top, I could walk it blind","Home was a mess, a loud, messy, wonderful mess","I'd trade everything I have for ten minutes in my own driveway","Used to complain about the commute, God, what a fool","The porch light was always on, always, in case somebody needed it","I left my keys on the hook by the door, wonder if they're still there","Dinner at six every night of my life, Mama never missed","The garden was just coming in, tomatoes, beans, all of it, wasted","Mama's quilt, I wish I'd grabbed Mama's quilt","It still smells like us in there, I bet, if I could go back","Could've sworn I locked the door, did I lock the door?"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=fresh|mood=sad",{"I keep walking toward home out of habit, and it's not there anymore","I wonder if somebody's sleeping in my bed, I hope so, I hope somebody is","Our wedding picture is still on the wall, I just know it","I can still hear the TV on in the living room, can't you?","My little girl's room, the stuffed rabbit on the pillow, her rabbit-","I wonder if the cat's still waiting by the window","I keep reaching for the phone to call Mama, and there's no phone, and there's no Mama-","The kitchen light, it was yellow, it made everything look warm, I miss yellow light","Sundays at Mamaw's, biscuits and gravy, her hands covered in flour","I left my Walkman on the dresser, I had a tape in it and everything","I'd give anything to hear my dad yell at the TV during the game","Our dog Biscuit would hear the truck from half a mile off, every time","I wasn't even supposed to leave the house that day, I only went for milk","My brother's bunk bed is still up, and nobody's in the bottom one","The last thing I did at home was forget to turn off the sprinkler, can you imagine","I wish I'd hugged her longer, I wish I'd hugged everybody longer","We had a swing on the maple out back, I bet it's still swinging","My mom hung up my school picture every year, crooked every year","Home smelled like laundry soap and bacon, home smelled like OUR home","I'd even take the arguments, the whole dinner table shouting, just to hear it","I never said goodbye to the house, I just locked the door and ran","Remember when the biggest problem was a curfew? A CURFEW?","I want my pillow, my own pillow, that's all I want, a pillow","I even miss the little things I used to complain about at home","Ohhh, I miss the sound of the ice cream truck going down our street","I kept all my pop bottle caps in a coffee can under the bed","I miss the smell of the rain on our gravel drive","I left my homework on the kitchen table, imagine caring about that","Does the porch swing still creak? Mama said she'd oil it, she never did"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=fresh|mood=warm",{"Christmas morning, remember Christmas morning? Everyone in their pajamas","Fourth of July, the whole family on the lawn, sparklers, laughing","My daddy's hands on the grill, I can see them now","Summer nights, catching lightning bugs in a jar, remember?","County fair, funnel cake, my grandpa winning me a stuffed bear","Friday night football, the whole town in the stands, the lights, the band","Daddy teaching me to fish at the creek behind our house, my first catfish","Grandma's quilt, every patch was somebody's old shirt, you could name them all","Thanksgiving, and every cousin was there, and the pies, the PIES","Skipping rocks on the pond, and Daddy always beat me, always","Church supper in the basement, casseroles on every table, laughter","Mamaw's lemon pie, nobody could make it like her, nobody","Christmas lights on the porch, and my brother falling off the ladder, hahaha"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=seasoned|mood=calm",{"Home's just a place, we'll make another one","Houses are wood and nails, family's what makes home","Sometimes I remember it, but I don't let myself stay in it long","Home's gone, so I carry it, little pieces, here and there","Home was nice, but this is where we are, so this is what we do","I keep a key to the front door in my pocket, doesn't open anything now","I think about the garden sometimes, the beans, the tomatoes, how green it was"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=seasoned|mood=grim",{"There's nothing to go back to, I know that, I do","Burned, I think, the house burned, I saw the smoke from the road","Don't talk to me about home, there's no use in it","Home's a word for people who still have one","Home was a house, houses burn"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|mood=funny",{"I miss my own toilet, heh, that's the real tragedy","Wouldn't you know it, I finally paid off the mortgage last spring","My wife wanted a pool, I said it's too much work, look at me now, heh","I'd give my right arm for a hot shower, no wait, I need that arm, my left","Never thought I'd miss my in-laws, heh, there's a first","Used to hate mowing the lawn, would you look at me now, I'd mow it twice","Mama's meatloaf was awful, and I'd eat three plates of it right now","I miss my La-Z-Boy more than I miss most of my relatives","My ex-wife kept the couch, and I kind of wish I'd fought for the couch"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=rescue",{"My station house, my locker, my coffee mug, I miss my coffee mug","The break room, the bad coffee, the bad jokes, all of it","I miss my own kitchen, my own stove, my own little life","The coffeemaker, God, the coffeemaker, it was a real good one"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","role=rescue_medical",{"My little apartment above the dry cleaner, I kept a plant in the window","My plants must be dead by now, I didn't water them, I didn't even say goodbye","My cat, my sweet cat, I hope somebody's feeding her"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","role=rescue_clergy",{"The sanctuary, the empty pews on a Tuesday, I'd sit and listen to quiet","Sunday service, the old hymns, how can I sing them now","Old Mrs Henley used to bring me banana bread every Sunday, I miss the bread","The bell in the steeple, I used to ring it, I wonder if anyone's ringing it"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","role=rescue_firefighter",{"The station, the pole, the guys, my guys","Station chili night, the guys, the stupid jokes, the sink full of dishes"}},
{"HOME_MEMORY","reg=law,swat",{"My badge is in my pocket, the house is on Elm, I wonder who's there","My wife's coffee, my kids' cereal, the whole sticky kitchen","My desk, my chair, my stupid stack of paperwork, I'd kill for it","Home was supposed to be where the bad day ended","Home had a porch light, and a wife who waited up, you ever have that","My kid's T-ball game, I missed half of them for the job, now I'd miss everything to see one","The recliner, the remote, a cold one, the ball game, sounds like heaven","My shift ended, I'd drive home, and the driveway was always lit, always","My locker still has my favorite mug in it","My locker at the station still has a sandwich in it, from the day before, I guess that's gone bad now"}},
